00:42:12.796 --> 00:42:14.525
Mr. Bradford!


00:42:17.268 --> 00:42:19.259
Mr. Bradford!


00:42:28.245 --> 00:42:29.974
Mr. Bradford!


00:42:37.454 --> 00:42:39.445
♪♪


00:43:10.087 --> 00:43:12.180
Mr. Bradford!


00:43:12.256 --> 00:43:14.520
Detective Crenshaw!


00:43:14.592 --> 00:43:16.583
Carlson Police!


00:43:18.662 --> 00:43:21.392
♪♪


00:43:21.465 --> 00:43:24.298
What are you doing? Who are you?


00:43:24.368 --> 00:43:26.563
Crenshaw, Carlson Police.


00:43:26.637 --> 00:43:28.537
What do you want?


00:43:28.606 --> 00:43:32.269
I'm talking to all the ranchers
in the area.


00:43:32.343 --> 00:43:34.334
You mind if I ask you
a few questions?


00:43:37.481 --> 00:43:40.416
You ever use a blacksmith
or a metal worker out here?


00:43:40.484 --> 00:43:43.146
- Maybe even a long time ago?
- Everybody does.


00:43:43.220 --> 00:43:47.054
I'm looking for the person
who might've made this link.


00:43:52.630 --> 00:43:55.599
Where'd you get this?


00:43:55.666 --> 00:43:57.600
You've seen this before?


00:43:57.668 --> 00:44:01.069
I have.


00:44:01.138 --> 00:44:03.732
I don't remember where.


00:44:05.643 --> 00:44:07.508
My wife would know.


00:44:07.578 --> 00:44:10.479
Well, can I talk to her?


00:44:10.547 --> 00:44:12.310
She's dead.


00:44:12.383 --> 00:44:14.283
I'm sorry.


00:44:14.351 --> 00:44:16.319
You better go now.


00:44:16.387 --> 00:44:18.753
If you can think of anything,
I'd appreciate a call.


00:45:44.975 --> 00:45:47.705
I just delete them.


00:45:47.778 --> 00:45:52.477
As soon as I get them, poof, gone.


00:46:05.496 --> 00:46:08.863
Your ass and your ass got it.


00:46:08.932 --> 00:46:11.264
All right. This boy
ain't pressing his luck.


00:46:34.158 --> 00:46:36.786
Remember that creep from
the Internet I told you about?


00:46:39.229 --> 00:46:41.129
A chain letter.


00:47:08.592 --> 00:47:11.254
You gotta pass it on.


00:47:23.307 --> 00:47:25.207
Come on, Rach.


00:47:42.459 --> 00:47:43.983
♪♪


00:47:44.061 --> 00:47:46.757
♪♪


00:48:24.534 --> 00:48:27.059
Rachael, it's me.
I found some stuff on the Internet,


00:48:27.137 --> 00:48:28.866
and I just- I'm really
scared right now.


00:48:28.939 --> 00:48:31.134
I just need you to call me back
as soon as you get this, okay?


00:48:31.208 --> 00:48:32.971
I just need to know
that you're okay.


00:48:33.043 --> 00:48:34.977
Call me back.


00:48:37.047 --> 00:48:38.981
♪♪


00:48:54.364 --> 00:48:56.798
♪♪


00:49:08.045 --> 00:49:09.808
Yeah?


00:49:09.880 --> 00:49:11.905
Neil, where's Rachael?
I can't get a hold of her.


00:49:11.982 --> 00:49:14.212
I- You know what?
I don't know.


00:49:14.284 --> 00:49:15.842
But I'm gonna take
a crack at it.


00:49:15.919 --> 00:49:18.683
Uh, she's probably balling
somebody about now.


00:49:18.755 --> 00:49:21.747
Neil, come on. I'm serious right now.
This is an emergency.


00:49:21.825 --> 00:49:24.419
Okay? She might be in danger.


00:49:25.996 --> 00:49:28.055
I just called the house.
Nobody picked up.


00:49:28.131 --> 00:49:30.065
Well, what do you want me
to do about that?


00:49:30.133 --> 00:49:32.067
- Where are your parents?
- Look, I don't know.


00:49:32.135 --> 00:49:35.366
They went to some benefit thing.
Jessie, can I call you back, please?


00:49:35.439 --> 00:49:37.737
I'm knee-deep in some action here.
I need to call you back.


00:49:37.808 --> 00:49:39.935
No, no, no, listen.
Neil, wait.


00:49:40.010 --> 00:49:42.342
Okay, just meet me at the house
as soon as you can, please?


00:49:42.412 --> 00:49:44.710
I'm going there right now,
and I'm too scared to go alone.


00:49:44.781 --> 00:49:47.045
So just meet me there, okay?
Please?


00:49:47.117 --> 00:49:50.109
Okay, I'll- I'll, uh-


00:49:50.187 --> 00:49:52.485
Yeah, I'll be-
I'll be right there.


00:50:27.491 --> 00:50:29.049
♪♪


00:51:48.939 --> 00:51:50.930
Neil?


00:52:21.471 --> 00:52:22.870
No!


00:52:24.474 --> 00:52:28.069
No! No!


00:54:52.155 --> 00:54:53.520
You got it.


00:54:53.590 --> 00:54:55.148
Listen, I-


00:54:55.225 --> 00:54:57.193
I really don't think
we need a profiler


00:54:57.260 --> 00:54:58.727
on this case right now.


00:55:00.830 --> 00:55:02.764
Yes, I am-


00:55:02.832 --> 00:55:05.232
What's his name?


00:55:05.302 --> 00:55:08.328
Wiggins? Fine. Fine.


00:55:16.012 --> 00:55:17.673
Jessie, listen,


00:55:17.747 --> 00:55:20.773
I'm really sorry
about your friend.


00:55:20.850 --> 00:55:23.546
I, uh- I can't imagine
what you've been going through.


00:55:26.189 --> 00:55:27.952
Listen, I just wanna ask you
a few questions


00:55:28.024 --> 00:55:29.855
so we can figure out
who's doing this.


00:55:29.926 --> 00:55:31.723
- Okay.
- Now,


00:55:31.795 --> 00:55:34.127
what made you
rush over here tonight?


00:55:34.197 --> 00:55:36.188
We all got these chain letters.


00:55:36.266 --> 00:55:38.734
Um...


00:55:38.802 --> 00:55:40.895
See?


00:55:45.709 --> 00:55:47.301
Who sent this?


00:55:47.377 --> 00:55:50.141
Jessie, what's going on?


00:55:50.213 --> 00:55:52.147
Rachael's dead.


00:55:52.215 --> 00:55:55.150
What? She's dead?


00:55:55.218 --> 00:55:59.314
Jessie, can you forward this
chain letter from your phone?


00:55:59.389 --> 00:56:01.323
Mm-hmm.


00:56:01.391 --> 00:56:03.052
I want you to send it
to this address.


00:56:03.126 --> 00:56:04.388
And then send it to me.


00:56:04.461 --> 00:56:07.555
- There's my e-mail.
- Are you sure?


00:56:07.630 --> 00:56:09.564
- Don't I have to send it to four people?
- No, no.


00:56:09.632 --> 00:56:11.156
- Because- And the thing is-
- Don't worry about it.


00:56:11.234 --> 00:56:12.792
I'll take care of it.


00:56:12.869 --> 00:56:14.894
Just send it to me.


00:56:14.971 --> 00:56:17.906
- Taylor.
- Excuse me.


00:56:20.543 --> 00:56:21.976
I want you to call the lab.


00:56:22.045 --> 00:56:24.104
Tell them I'm sending a chain
letter over there right now.


00:56:24.180 --> 00:56:25.442
See if they can trace it,


00:56:25.515 --> 00:56:27.449
or if it matches anything
we already have in the system.


00:56:27.517 --> 00:56:28.609
Right.


00:56:30.286 --> 00:56:32.880
Can either of you think
of anything else


00:56:32.956 --> 00:56:35.322
that I should know about?


00:56:35.392 --> 00:56:38.259
Drugs, uh, boyfriends, enemies?


00:56:39.929 --> 00:56:42.159
Um,


00:56:42.232 --> 00:56:44.166
yeah.


00:56:44.234 --> 00:56:46.862
There was a guy she met online.


00:56:46.936 --> 00:56:49.166
He was an older guy.


00:56:49.239 --> 00:56:52.106
She wasn't freaking out,
but he was sending her some weird stuff.


00:56:52.175 --> 00:56:55.576
- He was texting her all the time.
- Okay. Ever meet this guy?


00:56:55.645 --> 00:56:57.374
No.


00:56:57.447 --> 00:56:59.938
- All right.
- Okay.


00:57:00.016 --> 00:57:02.382
Okay, look-
look, that's- that's enough.


00:57:02.452 --> 00:57:04.943
- Oh, man.
- That's enough. Listen, take her inside.


00:57:05.021 --> 00:57:07.046
Take her inside.


00:57:07.123 --> 00:57:09.057
If you get any more chain letters


00:57:09.125 --> 00:57:11.787
or any suspicious texts,
I want you to call me right away.


00:57:11.861 --> 00:57:13.294
Send them to me.


00:57:13.363 --> 00:57:14.796
This is Stephanie.
She'll take care of you.


00:57:14.864 --> 00:57:17.025
- Jessie?
- Yeah.


00:57:25.642 --> 00:57:27.974
You okay, son?


00:57:28.044 --> 00:57:30.410
No. No, I'm not okay.


00:57:30.480 --> 00:57:33.608
It's all right.


00:57:33.683 --> 00:57:35.913
It's not- It's not-
It's not all right.


00:57:35.985 --> 00:57:38.647
- It's not all right.
- Let's go, son. Let's go.


00:57:52.001 --> 00:57:53.798
I hope you've solved the mystery.


00:57:53.870 --> 00:57:55.497
Detective Crenshaw.


00:57:57.307 --> 00:58:00.902
I knew it was you because
your name's on the plaques.


00:58:00.977 --> 00:58:02.467
I know who you are.


00:58:02.545 --> 00:58:05.776
- You do?
- Wiggins. Profiler.


00:58:05.849 --> 00:58:08.977
- Frank.
- I heard you transferred over.


00:58:09.052 --> 00:58:11.077
How do you like it so far?


00:58:11.154 --> 00:58:13.452
Big change from New York, huh?


00:58:13.523 --> 00:58:17.857
Yeah, it's- it's different,
but I'm- I'm adjusting to it.


00:58:17.927 --> 00:58:20.953
I've known about you
for quite a while.


00:58:21.030 --> 00:58:23.863
- 1996, I believe it was,
- Mmm.


00:58:23.933 --> 00:58:27.027
was the year that you broke
the Browning Brother cult.


00:58:27.103 --> 00:58:30.129
That was pretty impressive.


00:58:30.206 --> 00:58:32.174
Can I ask you a question,
Detective?


00:58:32.242 --> 00:58:34.540
You can ask.


00:58:34.611 --> 00:58:36.977
How'd you do it?


00:58:37.046 --> 00:58:39.173
Just instinct.


00:58:39.249 --> 00:58:43.117
Instincts. That's good.


00:58:43.186 --> 00:58:45.848
So, what do your instincts
tell you about this case?


00:58:48.791 --> 00:58:50.520
These chains are key.


00:58:52.362 --> 00:58:54.455
Always chains,
always the same kind.


00:58:54.531 --> 00:58:56.522
Most of them are in Evidence,


00:58:56.599 --> 00:58:59.295
but I- I held back a few.


00:58:59.369 --> 00:59:01.496
Mmm.


00:59:01.571 --> 00:59:05.405
Yeah, a little stamp on the side.
That's what you're talking about?


00:59:05.475 --> 00:59:08.501
Whatever it is, it's the key
to cracking this case.


00:59:08.578 --> 00:59:11.206
I profile people, not metal.


00:59:11.281 --> 00:59:13.408
Well, somehow,
it reminds me


00:59:13.483 --> 00:59:15.678
of a radical group
a few years back.


00:59:15.752 --> 00:59:17.379
Hold on, hold on.


00:59:17.453 --> 00:59:19.011
Keep talking.
What was their name?


00:59:19.088 --> 00:59:20.385
- Um...
- Something, uh...


00:59:20.456 --> 00:59:22.424
It was about technology,
anti-technology-


00:59:22.492 --> 00:59:23.550
Antech.


00:59:23.626 --> 00:59:25.059
- That's it.
- Yeah.


00:59:25.128 --> 00:59:26.925
- Okay. That's it. Antech.
- Yeah.


00:59:26.996 --> 00:59:29.556
They were apocalyptic
Luddites, right?


00:59:29.632 --> 00:59:31.361
They hated computers,
the Internet...


00:59:31.434 --> 00:59:32.992
But that was a group,
and I'm sure


00:59:33.069 --> 00:59:34.730
that this is the work
of a single guy.


00:59:34.804 --> 00:59:40.106
Do you remember, Detective,
the, uh, Unabomber?


00:59:40.176 --> 00:59:42.235
Uh, Ted Kaczynski, right?


00:59:42.312 --> 00:59:46.214
Went to Yale,
taught at Berkeley.


00:59:46.282 --> 00:59:48.216
He was a smart guy.


00:59:48.284 --> 00:59:50.218
He knew technology,
but he hated it.


00:59:50.286 --> 00:59:52.777
And if a guy is so anti-tech,


00:59:52.855 --> 00:59:55.722
why would he, uh,
send e-mails to people?


00:59:55.792 --> 00:59:57.726
I don't know.


00:59:57.794 --> 00:59:59.728
Why don't you tell me?


00:59:59.796 --> 01:00:03.027
Why? Why would someone
embrace something


01:00:03.099 --> 01:00:06.034
that they are so opposed to?


01:00:06.102 --> 01:00:09.594
Unless it's strategy.


01:00:09.672 --> 01:00:12.197
Fight fire with fire.


01:00:14.277 --> 01:00:17.212
That doesn't make sense.
That doesn't make any sense to me.


01:00:17.280 --> 01:00:20.772
Look, I mean, look at all the good
that technology has done.


01:00:20.850 --> 01:00:24.411
Breakthroughs in medicine,
instant communication all over the globe.


01:00:24.487 --> 01:00:26.819
- Detective, you don't get it, do you?
- Helps save innocent lives.


01:00:26.889 --> 01:00:28.720
They don't like technology.


01:00:28.791 --> 01:00:32.557
It doesn't matter about
the result or the application.


01:00:32.629 --> 01:00:35.097
They don't like technology.


01:00:35.164 --> 01:00:37.257
That's it.
Please, do me a favor.


01:00:37.333 --> 01:00:40.598
Allow me to take these photos
for a couple of days.


01:00:40.670 --> 01:00:42.638
You know, I got one plaque
in my whole life,


01:00:42.705 --> 01:00:44.263
and they spelled my name wrong.


01:00:44.340 --> 01:00:46.467
Two G's, not one.


01:00:50.413 --> 01:00:52.506
Hey, Michael, it's Jess.


01:00:52.582 --> 01:00:54.914
I've been doing some research
on the chain letters.


01:00:54.984 --> 01:00:57.179
Call me back when you get this.
I'm headed home now.


01:01:47.470 --> 01:01:49.938
How can someone do this?


01:02:02.719 --> 01:02:05.153
Someone's tracking us.


01:03:17.059 --> 01:03:19.459
Huh? Huh?


01:04:44.480 --> 01:04:45.811
Hey.


01:04:50.920 --> 01:04:53.411
Hey, buddy. How you doing?


01:04:53.489 --> 01:04:55.548
How do you think I'm doing?


01:04:57.927 --> 01:05:01.192
- I miss her, too, Neil.
- Yeah.


01:05:01.264 --> 01:05:03.198
Yeah.


01:05:03.266 --> 01:05:04.893
So, uh-


01:05:04.967 --> 01:05:07.765
You wanna tell me what
this meeting is about, guys?


01:05:07.837 --> 01:05:10.829
I mean, you're not gonna stop
any of these killings, Jessie.


01:05:10.907 --> 01:05:13.899
You send out five chain letters,
and then five pop up everywhere.


01:05:13.976 --> 01:05:16.069
I know. I know.
Just listen to me, okay?


01:05:16.145 --> 01:05:18.670
There's a person behind this,
and I think I know what he's doing.


01:05:18.748 --> 01:05:21.182
- He's tracking us online.
- Tracking us how?


01:05:21.250 --> 01:05:23.946
There's a virus that I found
in my phone and in the e-mail, okay?


01:05:24.020 --> 01:05:25.954
The virus is a tracker.
We all have it.


01:05:26.022 --> 01:05:28.217
That's how he knows whether
or not we pass it on.


01:05:28.291 --> 01:05:30.691
That's fucking crazy.
How could he know where we live? How?


01:05:30.760 --> 01:05:33.627
It's easy, okay? Everything you have
is connected to a bill you pay, right?


01:05:33.696 --> 01:05:35.755
And all the companies who bill you
have your addresses.


01:05:35.831 --> 01:05:37.093
It's not that hard.


01:05:37.166 --> 01:05:39.100
I never even thought about that.


01:05:39.168 --> 01:05:41.796
But why us, huh?
Why us out of everybody?


01:05:41.871 --> 01:05:44.101
Because he's a fucking
psychopath, Michael!


01:05:44.173 --> 01:05:46.107
Why did Jeffrey Dahmer kill people?


01:05:46.175 --> 01:05:48.302
- Why did O.J. slash his wife?
- What are you saying?


01:05:48.377 --> 01:05:50.777
- What do you think I'm saying?
- Guys, come on. Stop.


01:05:50.846 --> 01:05:52.973
No. This is not
on you guys, all right?


01:05:53.049 --> 01:05:55.574
- Who do you think got the first message?
- Who did he send it to then?


01:05:55.651 --> 01:05:57.881
Me. He sent me
the message, all right?


01:05:57.954 --> 01:05:59.478
I- He said it was a game.


01:05:59.555 --> 01:06:02.080
And I sent it to you guys.
You know how that feels?


01:06:02.158 --> 01:06:04.217
You wanna know what that-
Fuck it. All right.


01:06:04.293 --> 01:06:06.488
- I'll show you what that fucking feels like.
- What are you doing?


01:06:06.562 --> 01:06:08.792
- Neil, what are you doing?
- I'm gonna show you.


01:06:08.864 --> 01:06:11.128
I'm gonna fucking show you what it's like
to be in my fucking shoes.


01:06:11.200 --> 01:06:12.565
What the fuck are you doing?


01:06:12.635 --> 01:06:14.398
What are you doing?
Give me your phone.


01:06:14.470 --> 01:06:16.233
I sent you the message.


01:06:16.305 --> 01:06:18.830
You got it.


01:06:26.415 --> 01:06:27.643
All right. It's fine.


01:06:28.651 --> 01:06:30.710
You fucking shit.


01:06:34.857 --> 01:06:36.984
- Stop!
- Stop!


01:06:37.059 --> 01:06:39.289
- You threaten my life?
- This isn't on you!


01:06:39.362 --> 01:06:42.092
This is on me, all right?
This is on me!


01:06:42.164 --> 01:06:45.099
Everybody's fucking dead,
and you pull a fucking gun out on us?


01:06:51.007 --> 01:06:53.840
- Oh, fuck.
- What?


01:06:53.909 --> 01:06:56.002
- He fucking sent me another chain letter.
- What?


01:06:56.078 --> 01:06:59.570
Fucking break the chain,
and you will die, man.


01:07:01.083 --> 01:07:03.881
Man, he's watching us.
He is watching us.


01:07:03.953 --> 01:07:06.353
Fuck you, Neil.
What are you saying? Where is he?


01:07:06.422 --> 01:07:09.323
- He's here. He's watching us.
- We gotta do something now.


01:07:09.392 --> 01:07:12.225
Okay, so the way this works
is you die if you delete it, right?


01:07:12.294 --> 01:07:15.388
The chain letter said
we had 24 hours.


01:07:15.464 --> 01:07:17.694
I don't wanna die.


01:07:17.767 --> 01:07:20.895
I'm just gonna send the fucking message
to people that I hate, right?


01:07:20.970 --> 01:07:22.904
I mean, if they die,
big fucking deal.


01:07:22.972 --> 01:07:24.667
- Too bad for them.
- You're fucking tripping right now.


01:07:24.740 --> 01:07:27.004
- Just chill out for a second.
- Hey, I sent the message to you,


01:07:27.076 --> 01:07:28.907
didn't I?


01:07:30.546 --> 01:07:33.037
Fuck you guys, man.
I'm fucking outta here.


01:07:33.115 --> 01:07:36.209
So listen to me. I know how
we can pass these on, okay?


01:07:36.285 --> 01:07:38.753
And then once it's over,
we just have to get rid of our phones


01:07:38.821 --> 01:07:40.220
and our e-mail addresses, okay?


01:07:40.289 --> 01:07:42.587
Whatever.


01:07:42.658 --> 01:07:45.718
What the fuck
does it matter now, huh?


01:07:59.909 --> 01:08:02.400
You've received chain mail.


01:08:06.816 --> 01:08:09.410
Why the fuck do you keep
sending these to me, man?


01:08:09.485 --> 01:08:12.181
I'm doing everything you want me to do.
I keep sending them on.


01:08:13.622 --> 01:08:14.987
Fucker!


01:08:19.962 --> 01:08:22.453
You've received chain mail.


01:08:22.531 --> 01:08:25.022
What the fuck
you want me to do?


01:08:25.101 --> 01:08:27.797
I've sent off these goddamn chain letters
to everyone I fucking know.


01:08:29.472 --> 01:08:31.235
You've received chain mail.


01:08:31.307 --> 01:08:34.140
Fucking relax, man.
I just gotta take...


01:08:34.210 --> 01:08:36.974
I gotta take a deep
fucking breath.


01:08:38.681 --> 01:08:40.273
I just gotta think
what I'm gonna do.


01:08:40.349 --> 01:08:43.375
You've received chain mail.


01:08:43.452 --> 01:08:46.979
Fucking Rachael.


01:08:50.392 --> 01:08:51.950
You've received chain mail.


01:08:52.027 --> 01:08:54.621
All right.


01:08:54.697 --> 01:08:57.962
